Q3. What is the difference between List, Set, and Map? Why does Map not extend the Collection interface?

List, Set, and Queue are interfaces that extend the Collection interface and represent collections of individual elements.

List allows duplicates and maintains positional ordering, while Set represents unique elements.

Map is also part of the Java Collections Framework, 
but it is a separate interface hierarchy because it represents key-value mappings rather than a collection of individual elements.
Its operations are based on keys and values, such as put(), get(), and containsKey(), so it does not naturally fit the Collection abstraction.

