Q4. You need to maintain users in the order they were inserted, prevent duplicate users, and perform fast lookup by user ID. 
Which collection(s) would you choose and why?


I would use a LinkedHashMap<UserId, User>.
It gives me unique user IDs because Map keys are unique, 
maintains insertion order because LinkedHashMap maintains a linked ordering of entries, 
and provides O(1) average-time lookup by user ID through hashing. 
If I only needed uniqueness and insertion order without key-based lookup, I would use LinkedHashSet instead.


